  "title": "Traditional sugarplums",
  "subtitle": "spiced nut and fruit balls rolled in caster sugar",
  "excerpt": "Traditional sugarplums are not made from plums at all but take their name from the Old English word for any dried fruit or sugar sweet. This version blends dates, almonds, pistachios, and candied peel with warm spices and a little orange blossom water, then rolls the shaped balls in caster sugar to give a sweet, sparkling coat. They are a natural preserve that keeps for weeks and makes a lovely Christmas gift.",
